From: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: bridge: read the ECM helpers' state under RCU

Two helpers that the ECM patches add are called by ECM under RCU or in
softirq, and lockdep reports both (IPQ5018, first accelerated flows):

- br_dev_is_vlan_filter_enabled() (0966) says its caller holds the RCU
  read lock, and ECM calls it from the post-routing hook under
  rcu_read_lock(), but it took the VLAN groups with br_vlan_group() and
  nbp_vlan_group(), which expect RTNL ("suspicious
  rcu_dereference_protected() usage", br_private.h:1620 and 1626). Use
  their _rcu variants.

- br_fdb_entry_refresh() (0960) looked the port up with
  br_port_get_rcu() before its own rcu_read_lock(); ECM calls it from
  the NSS stats sync in NAPI context with no RCU section open
  ("suspicious rcu_dereference_check() usage", br_private.h:457). Take
  the lock first.

Signed-off-by: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
---
--- a/net/bridge/br_fdb.c
+++ b/net/bridge/br_fdb.c
@@ -1156,16 +1156,18 @@ void br_fdb_update(struct net_bridge *br
 void br_fdb_entry_refresh(struct net_device *dev, const char *addr, __u16 vid)
 {
 	struct net_bridge_fdb_entry *fdb;
-	struct net_bridge_port *p = br_port_get_rcu(dev);
+	struct net_bridge_port *p;
 
+	rcu_read_lock();
+	p = br_port_get_rcu(dev);
 	if (!p || p->state == BR_STATE_DISABLED)
-		return;
+		goto out;
 
-	rcu_read_lock();
 	fdb = fdb_find_rcu(&p->br->fdb_hash_tbl, addr, vid);
 	if (likely(fdb)) {
 		fdb->updated = jiffies;
 	}
+out:
 	rcu_read_unlock();
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(br_fdb_entry_refresh);
--- a/net/bridge/br_vlan.c
+++ b/net/bridge/br_vlan.c
@@ -961,7 +961,7 @@ int br_dev_is_vlan_filter_enabled(struct
 			return -ENOENT;
 		}
 
-		vg = br_vlan_group(netdev_priv(dev));
+		vg = br_vlan_group_rcu(netdev_priv(dev));
 	} else if (dev->priv_flags & IFF_BRIDGE_PORT) {
 		/*
 		 * It's a bridge port
@@ -977,7 +977,7 @@ int br_dev_is_vlan_filter_enabled(struct
 
 		p = br_port_get_rcu(dev);
 		if (p)
-			vg = nbp_vlan_group(p);
+			vg = nbp_vlan_group_rcu(p);
 	} else {
 		/*
 		 * Neither a bridge device or port
